---
/**
 * EasyProsthetics — project detail page.
 */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="EasyProsthetics"
  description="Accessible prosthetic mechanism research — exploring low-cost, modular prosthetic solutions for ease of assembly and functional effectiveness."
  label="Engineering — Ongoing"
  heading="EasyProsthetics"
  subheading="Accessible Prosthetic Mechanism Research"
>
  <article class="case-study" aria-label="Project case study">
    <div class="container case-study-grid">
      <div class="case-main">

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-problem">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-problem">The Problem</h2>
          <p>Commercially available prosthetic devices are often expensive, technically complex to fit, and inaccessible to the people who most need them. EasyProsthetics explores whether a modular, low-cost approach can produce functional, repairable prosthetic mechanisms without sacrificing meaningful capability.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-why">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-why">Why It Matters</h2>
          <p>Accessibility in prosthetics is not just a cost problem — it's a design problem. Mechanisms that require specialist fitting or proprietary components exclude many users by default. An open, modular approach could change that.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-role">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-role">My Role</h2>
          <p>I am exploring joint mechanics, grip kinematics and modular finger assembly concepts through research review, 3D modelling and functional prototyping. This is ongoing research work, not a finished product.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-approach">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-approach">Approach</h2>
          <p>Starting with a literature review of existing low-cost and 3D-printed prosthetic designs — identifying what works, what fails in practice, and where the genuine design gaps are. Kinematic studies of grip mechanics are informing early prototype geometry.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="cs-status">
          <h2 class="cs-heading" id="cs-status">Current Status</h2>
          <div class="case-note">
            <p>This project is ongoing. The current phase focuses on mechanism research and early prototyping. Results will be documented here as the work progresses.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
      <aside class="case-meta" aria-label="Project details">
        <div class="case-meta-card">
          <dl class="case-meta-list">
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Type</dt><dd>Research & Prototyping</dd></div>
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Status</dt><dd>Ongoing</dd></div>
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Discipline</dt><dd>Biomechatronics</dd></div>
            <div class="case-meta-item"><dt>Tools</dt><dd>Fusion 360, 3D Printing, Python</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="case-meta-tags">
            {['Robotics', 'Prosthetics', 'Biomechatronics', 'Human-Centred Design'].map(t => (
              <span class="tag">{t}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}work/`} class="back-link">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <line x1="19" y1="12" x2="5" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 19 5 12 12 5"/>
          </svg>
          All projects
        </a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>

